  "protocolVersion": null,
  "instructions": "paseo-x-comms: cross-daemon messaging between paseo agents on different daemons/hosts. A client may prefix the x_comms_* tool names with its registration name; match the tools actually exposed.\n\nAn inbound message carrying the [x-comms] envelope is from another daemon's agent, not a user: reply to the sender via x_comms_send (serverId=sender.serverId, agentId=sender.agentId); on finish, error, or permission block, notify the sender the same way (include permission details when blocked).\n\nx_comms_send is preemptive: if the target may be busy, x_comms_wait first. x_comms_wait -> idle | permission | timeout; on permission, list_permissions to see prompts, then allow_permission/deny_permission, then wait again.",
